# What the image must not carry.
#
# Read this next to .gitignore rather than copying it. The two have opposite
# jobs: git excludes the diary because the repository is public, and the image
# MUST include it or the site deploys with nothing in it. The paths that git
# ignores and this file deliberately keeps are listed at the bottom.

.git
.gitignore

# Secrets. Next copies .env files into .next/standalone on purpose, so keeping
# them out of the build context is the only thing that keeps them out of the
# image. Runtime configuration comes from `fly secrets`.
.env
.env.*

# Built on the host, for the host. node_modules holds macOS binaries for
# better-sqlite3 that cannot run on linux; the image builds its own.
node_modules
.next
.next-prod
*.tsbuildinfo

# Tooling and noise.
.agents
.claude
.vscode
.DS_Store
npm-debug.log*
scratch
drizzle.config.ts

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately NOT ignored, though .gitignore excludes every one of them:
#
#   data/diary.db            the diary itself
#   public/posters/*         artwork
#   public/people/*          headshots
#   public/shots/*           photographs taken at the cinema
#
# They reach the image from this machine and nowhere else, because they are
# not in the repository. `scripts/check-shippable.ts` runs during the build and
# fails if they are missing, so an empty site cannot be deployed by accident.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
